                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0aa93498-528c-37af-b43b-7975500126f9",
                        "entry_id": "38b991e7-dc54-3a16-929c-6d5e429f90a3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. замыкать"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6083ad7-e34e-4c22-83e0-9083c8a1e9e4",
                                "sense_id": "0aa93498-528c-37af-b43b-7975500126f9",
                                "text": "Это обстоятельство указывает на то, что реакция прошла с замыканием кольца и образованием α, α'-диметилпирролин-α-карбоновой кислоты."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bad2454b-9bc4-496d-af03-f4beff9da414",
                                "sense_id": "0aa93498-528c-37af-b43b-7975500126f9",
                                "text": "Самоуглубление здесь, в области знания, есть не замыкание духа, а, напротив, его расширение, освобождение его от всяческой узости, обусловливающей его слепоту."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a19fcf9c-7539-3c5e-b851-65464fa02ff7",
                        "entry_id": "38b991e7-dc54-3a16-929c-6d5e429f90a3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "эл.-техн. то же, что короткое замыкание; не предусмотренное нормальными условиями работы соединение точек электрической цепи, имеющих различные потенциалы, друг с другом или с другими цепями через пренебрежимо малое сопротивление"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "61322186-364e-3c48-8ca8-23921c3f5a74",
                        "entry_id": "38b991e7-dc54-3a16-929c-6d5e429f90a3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "лингв. вид подчинительной связи, при котором аффикс или служебное слово, семантически относясь к стержневому слову, ставится при первом слове словосочетания, объединяя тем самым в единое целое как простые, так и сложные словосочетания"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ca3c100-127a-34a8-baa8-5ce835fd141d",
                        "entry_id": "38b991e7-dc54-3a16-929c-6d5e429f90a3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "прогр. совокупность блока кода и данных того контекста исполнения программы, в котором этот блок порождён"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64acd49e-6913-45a8-8399-2032db3d3592",
                        "source_entry_id": "38b991e7-dc54-3a16-929c-6d5e429f90a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "непреднамеренное соединение в электрической цепи",
                        "target_lang_word": "short circuit",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "short circuit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8887b282-8943-35a5-aac5-2090560b19fc",
                                        "entry_id": "22380fc8-0138-303b-be44-2ca9d47296d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A usually unintentional connection of low resistance or impedance in a circuit such that excessive and often damaging current flows in it."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "short circuit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ba1a042-64cf-391d-9272-3e1f68943003",
                                        "entry_id": "b3de01d7-b555-3e6e-83ac-6ed22a5ad765",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause a short circuit in."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cee0e76-cb58-4790-8e40-1f69ace73125",
                                                "sense_id": "3ba1a042-64cf-391d-9272-3e1f68943003",
                                                "text": "The Jewish Community Relations Council does work on racism and multicultural issues, but they don't address anti-Arab racism in this work. They see that as 'political.' It's like they have a short-circuit inside them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1dfb543-6cb4-4d8c-96ab-d7dd40b8c597",
                                                "sense_id": "3ba1a042-64cf-391d-9272-3e1f68943003",
                                                "text": "Just the thought of being in a crisis that we cannot buy, build or invest our way out of seems to create some kind of collective mental short-circuit. This mix of ignorance, denial and unawareness is the very heart of the problem"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d8197af-4aca-45b4-bafc-d940209abe40",
                                                "sense_id": "3ba1a042-64cf-391d-9272-3e1f68943003",
                                                "text": "In the motor control room aft, a crewman crashed against the main electrical switchboard, short-circuiting it with his body, and all power aboard was lost."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29c8c4a6-74ec-3f93-acd5-93861fb6300e",
                                        "entry_id": "b3de01d7-b555-3e6e-83ac-6ed22a5ad765",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To undergo a short circuit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "839f6550-83b5-3045-98de-f9fe5e59bfbe",
                                        "entry_id": "b3de01d7-b555-3e6e-83ac-6ed22a5ad765",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To force termination of an ongoing process before its natural conclusion, by bypassing one or more intermediary steps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e18c9fa5-37f0-4212-93a5-212f8d4387d8",
                                                "sense_id": "839f6550-83b5-3045-98de-f9fe5e59bfbe",
                                                "text": "[H]is temporarily successful attempt to smear Redfield is an effort to short-circuit the narrative into premature and mistaken resolution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5588ab0-9926-4f20-bb53-4f702a8db7dc",
                                                "sense_id": "839f6550-83b5-3045-98de-f9fe5e59bfbe",
                                                "text": "You do not need to follow your entire sales cycle if the customer wants to short-circuit it for you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dd8c51e-db1c-4bc4-a619-73fd4e5723f1",
                                                "sense_id": "839f6550-83b5-3045-98de-f9fe5e59bfbe",
                                                "text": "My mother, determined to short-circuit my outcry, would match my objections by pointing out an inherent reward for doing such work."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99bb2244-3332-3960-a4a5-718496d26438",
                                        "entry_id": "b3de01d7-b555-3e6e-83ac-6ed22a5ad765",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To impede or disrupt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "706b9bed-db03-4669-892b-d86b590b4912",
                                                "sense_id": "99bb2244-3332-3960-a4a5-718496d26438",
                                                "text": "At times, the Knicks’ offense looked short-circuited. Anthony, despite his cold hand, kept shooting. / “They all feel good, to be honest with you,” Anthony said. “It wasn’t long, it wasn’t short, they were bouncing off the rim, they were chippers, the same shot I hit all the time so I can’t stop taking my shots.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cee3bb3-b8d4-316b-8682-e105342237be",
                                        "entry_id": "b3de01d7-b555-3e6e-83ac-6ed22a5ad765",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bypass, especially by overhastiness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a093a5f-b5de-4480-af80-4a7dc5fb000a",
                                                "sense_id": "9cee3bb3-b8d4-316b-8682-e105342237be",
                                                "text": "By insisting that \"style\" is the only way to exert your undeserving self upon the world these books short-circuit the chance for, and even the need for, the possibility of change in the lives of people or the culture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb686003-2a4d-4876-8d46-9fbf5fa5907d",
                                                "sense_id": "9cee3bb3-b8d4-316b-8682-e105342237be",
                                                "text": "By multiplying interpretive registers, however, Baudelaire's text short-circuits the desire for identification as well as erodes any rigid allegorical mapping."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "edc3edf0-5d1b-3110-98f2-d60c646ee1f4",
                                        "entry_id": "b3de01d7-b555-3e6e-83ac-6ed22a5ad765",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To terminate a loop before the declared termination condition is met, or a conditional before all conditions have been tested for."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f99b13d8-f885-4361-92d6-d5a577e1beb9",
                                                "sense_id": "edc3edf0-5d1b-3110-98f2-d60c646ee1f4",
                                                "text": "The \"Demand\" is done to ensure that you have indeed been granted this permission before using the \"Assert\" to short-circuit the stackwalk."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0610999c-a899-45b6-b275-0090198077dd",
                                                "sense_id": "edc3edf0-5d1b-3110-98f2-d60c646ee1f4",
                                                "text": "For example, to short-circuit the \"LoggedIn()\" or \"LogIn()\" \"if\" conditional, replace the \"Or\" with \"OrElse\" and the statement is interpreted to mean \"if not logged in, then log in\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80730452-d914-4843-9322-e9e51597c6aa",
                                                "sense_id": "edc3edf0-5d1b-3110-98f2-d60c646ee1f4",
                                                "text": "If you would like to short-circuit, you must replace \"And\" with the \"AndAlso\" keyword and \"Or\" with the \"OrElse\" keyword, as follows...."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
